  id: W5_07
  era: Adopted 26 November 1949; in force 26 January 1950
  title: The Constitution of India
  text: The Constitution of India. The Constituent Assembly, chaired by Rajendra Prasad, with B. R. Ambedkar leading the drafting committee, debated the Constitution for nearly three years. The original copies were hand-written by Prem Behari Narain Raizada and illuminated by artists of Santiniketan under Nandalal Bose. Its Preamble promises justice, liberty, equality and fraternity. It is one of the longest written national constitutions in the world. Universal adult suffrage gave every citizen over twenty-one the vote, regardless of caste, religion, gender or wealth.
